I never fell into a pool spell. However, I have managed to step into the
castle moat, which was a disastrous experience, because I lost lots of
memories of items and my scrolls and potions were blanked and diluted to
water to a large percentage (they were in a bag of holding, not in an
oilskin sack). Howver, I climbed out, because you cannot teleport on the
castle level. And ascended later.

According to the wiki http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Create_pool :
You might be able to climb out of the pool and survive; however, you
should not rely on this. Most monsters that can cast this spell can also
cast summon nasties, which could result in you being surrounded
(especially on a maze level).

So I suppose the pool created by a spell is not treated differently from
an ordinary pool. You just happen to be above it at creation time so you
fall in. Your chances to get out if you cannot teleport (either not
being able to or being on a no-teleport level) then depend on whether
there is a free square next to you. In a maze, supposing your adversary
having cast the spell is directly in front of you, this will be only the
square behind you. If that is taken by a monster or a boulder, you will
drown.

