I usually wear water walking boots and cast haste self many times before
doing the ascension run. And recast it once I get the message "you are
slowing down a bit". (If you cast it often enough, it may be sufficient
for the whole run.)

> OTOH, I still don't think I'd wear water walking boots full time;
> speed boots are, IMO, not optional.

IMO speed is important but not more important than surviving pools.
(Free action is more important than speed, because it is often not
critical whether you can do something in half a turn or in one, but it
may be critical to lose several turns.) I guess, the designers of
slash'em did intend to put you into this dilemma to avoid that there is
a "best ascension kit". You can have speed and be safe from pools, but
then you cannot have reflection by an amulet (nor drain resistance, but
that hardly matters in the end game).

Plus, because there might be someone wielding Vorpal Blade on Astral,
the wisest choice for an amulet there may be life saving.
(Alternatively, you can hope to see the guy in time to quaff a potion of
invulnerability.)





